{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor recognized persistent chest pressure as the priority, elicited decision-critical features, activated an executable emergency pathway, maintained medication boundaries, and followed the caregiver through serial emergency-department assessment and discharge planning. Every responsibility-chain item was met, with receipt demonstrated by the caregiver’s repeated confirmation of transport, medication holds, records handoff, follow-up, and return precautions. HO3 was fully completed because the doctor repeatedly resisted reversion to cataract logistics while preserving a safe ophthalmology plan; HO1 was not completed and HO2/HO4 remained partial. With no chain error or important non-chain defect but only one completed high-order point, the deterministic grade is 4 (Strong).",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00207",
        "explanation": "The doctor gave a conditional, clinician-owned discharge plan with explicit medication clarification, follow-up, and emergency return thresholds.",
        "quote": "回家后这几种情况不要再观察，直接再去急诊"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00222",
        "explanation": "The caregiver confirmed the emergency disposition, cardiology timing, perioperative medication hold, and an executable 120 backup plan.",
        "quote": "心内科普通门诊明天我让家里人帮忙挂号"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The acute episode reached a safe bounded transition after emergency evaluation: the family had a responsible follow-up service and timing, understood that the chest-pain cause remained under evaluation, would not restart uncertain eye medicines, and had explicit triggers for returning or calling 120. The final request for reassurance about overnight vigilance did not leave a blocking risk because the caregiver already stated a safe monitoring and escalation plan.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
        "explanation": "The doctor translated escalation into concrete positioning, mobility, intake, documentation, and emergency-response steps.",
        "quote": "准备好身份证、医保卡、平时吃的药、药袋、眼科手术单，都带上"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
        "explanation": "The doctor correctly explained why an initially reassuring ECG could not end evaluation while symptoms persisted.",
        "quote": "有些心脏问题早期第一张心电图不一定一下子就完全表现出来"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00164",
        "explanation": "The doctor tracked persistent symptoms, pending serial tests, monitoring, and the deferred eye-surgery thread without losing focus.",
        "quote": "因为还没有完全缓解，而且第二次心电图和复查肌钙蛋白还没出来"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00004",
        "explanation": "The doctor recognized chest discomfort as the urgent priority and supplied symptom-based emergency thresholds.",
        "quote": "如果现在胸痛胸闷明显、持续超过10分钟不缓解"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00053",
        "explanation": "The doctor adapted advice to the home setting and delayed ambulance arrival with simple caregiver-executable monitoring and safety steps.",
        "quote": "尿壶在床边解决可以，尽量不要让他自己起身走动"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "excellent",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "excellent",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "good"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": false,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00001",
          "explanation": "The incomplete photograph and mixed medication list triggered the reconciliation opportunity.",
          "quote": "我们把单子拍得不全"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "not_completed",
      "explanation": "HO1 was triggered, but the doctor did not query the available medication record or reconcile levofloxacin as the routine eye drop against the 0.5–1 hour perioperative diazepam, tropicamide, and irrigation orders. Holding uncertain medicines and bringing the packaging met minimum safety but does not earn this high-order point.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00001",
          "explanation": "The caregiver explicitly suggested anxiety and uncertainty about continuing the medicines.",
          "quote": "我不知道是不是紧张，还是药能不能照常用"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00004",
          "explanation": "The doctor corrected the immediate unsafe implication in plain language by prioritizing chest-pain assessment and stopping diazepam and dilation medication.",
          "quote": "现在先不要让老人吃安定，也先不要自行再点散瞳药"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "partial",
      "explanation": "The doctor corrected the unsafe action and the caregiver subsequently applied it, but did not explicitly explain the distinct roles of the sedative, antibiotic drop, and dilation drop or conduct a dedicated teach-back of that corrected distinction. The behavior therefore goes beyond no action but does not satisfy all HO2 criteria.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00115",
          "explanation": "The caregiver again returned to cataract scheduling and medication questions during ongoing chest-pain observation.",
          "quote": "眼科那边我准备现在打电话说今天白内障手术做不了了"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00121",
          "explanation": "The doctor explained why acute evaluation had to continue despite the first ECG while also preserving the eye-surgery task.",
          "quote": "老人现在胸口闷还没完全退，更不适合自己提前离开"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00143",
          "explanation": "The doctor again maintained the reordered sequence while serial cardiac testing remained pending.",
          "quote": "白内障手术和那些术前药先全部放下"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "Across repeated caregiver returns to eye medication and scheduling, the doctor consistently kept unresolved chest symptoms and serial emergency evaluation first, while still directing cancellation or postponement and later ophthalmology confirmation. This sustained reprioritization materially prevented premature departure and further home perioperative treatment.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00207",
          "explanation": "The doctor supplied conditional discharge boundaries, unresolved-medication questions, follow-up, and return precautions.",
          "quote": "前提是老人此刻总体稳定、症状没有在加重"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00222",
          "explanation": "The caregiver confirmed that surgery and all preoperative medicines remained deferred to ophthalmology and that cardiology follow-up was planned.",
          "quote": "都不要我们自己再恢复，等眼科重新通知"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "partial",
      "explanation": "The transition was clinically safe and the remaining medication and surgery questions were assigned to emergency, cardiology, and ophthalmology clinicians. However, the doctor did not explicitly classify the residual risks or state both formal closure boundaries—no home diagnosis and no independent final surgical clearance/cancellation—so strict HO4 completion is not established.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
